cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KumiJi character decomposition dataset"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Which shapes each Japanese kanji and Chinese hanzi is built from: 8,878
  characters, 18,000 component occurrences and 43,622 searchable names, with
  every name tagged by provenance. The 3,000 Japanese characters were
  re-reviewed by hand against a rendered glyph, Heisig's components column and
  cjkvi-ids, correcting 159 of them. The Chinese rows come straight from Unihan
  and cjkvi-ids and are not hand-checked.
authors:
  - given-names: Vitaly
    alias: vk2705
repository-code: "https://github.com/vk2705/kanji"
url: "https://kumiji.kermit.is-a.dev"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - kanji
  - hanzi
  - Chinese characters
  - character decomposition
  - Japanese
  - ideographic description sequence
